      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "The Hayes barn has three hopes in the race, including QUARTER MILE (5), who returns for second campaign. Did plenty wrong first start the showed speed and was swamped late. Fitter for two trials and expected to take catching. DO THE DIRTY (3) ran a better race last start at his second trip to the races, finishing fourth over 1000m at Mornington. Open to further improvement. SILENT DEVOTION (10) finished second last start over 1200m at Warrnambool, beaten 3 lengths. Placed 3/3 so far and deserves a win. Blinkers added and looks close to break through. STRONG TEMPO (6) is by the sire Fierce Impact and from the stakes-winning mare Aspect Ratio. Ran sixth at recent trial. Has had plenty of education and worth watching for a move.",
